# This clone lives inside the Drive corpus: Drive delivers its files to the
# second machine AND a git pull there writes them again. Both copies must be
# byte-identical, or bisync sees "changed on both sides" and parks one as
# .conflictN - on 2026-10-09 that took upload-ledger.ps1 and conflict-names.ps1
# away from this machine (LF here, CRLF from the pull on the P16) and both
# watchers crash-looped once restarted. Fixed line endings make every
# checkout identical, independent of core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=crlf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
